{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-31cf-76dc-908e-8d9be7f53585","id":"01a1a63a-a20f-722b-9676-8739582dbc46","idempotency_key":"468babf10dac6ffb9ae6523ee633c198f553b3bb31b5fa6f6c80d74a2ee412c9","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:42Z","payload":{"note":"The Play tab's tournament panel is a real UI now. The create control is a form (name, format, comma-separated competitors) instead of a button with four hardcoded models, so Swiss and knockout are reachable as well as round robin. The panel renders the open round's pairings with their results plus the projected standings, keeps a log of what was created/stepped/paused, and Export PGN downloads the combined file. Routes behind it: POST /api/ai/tournaments, GET list and detail (which carries the projected standings), POST {id}/step|pause|resume, GET {id}/pgn. cdp_tournament.js -> AI_TOURNAMENT_PASS with 'created UI cup (double-round-robin)', 'step: started 2 game(s)', two pairings, four standings rows, 'pause: paused' and match.pgn. Two real bugs came out of writing that check: the detail was only refreshed when the selection changed, so a Step showed no pairings until you reselected; and my own download spy was uninstalled before the async export resolved, which reported a working button as broken.","target":"t-a994"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
